From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:22:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(todo): durable, always-loaded todo list for long work

todo_list was deferred behind tool_search and lived only in memory, rebuilt
from the transcript (results over a size cap dropped), so a long chat lost its
plan at compactions, fresh per-message agents and restarts, and agents rarely
used it.

- Always loaded: todo_list is no longer in the default tools.tool_search.defer
  list, and its description says when to use it (more than a few steps, every
  delegation plan, every 'all N items' job) and that the list survives.
- Durable: every write is a read-modify-write of a session_todos row in
  state.db in one transaction. A read walks the compression lineage back to
  the newest stored row, so the list follows a chat across every compaction,
  fresh agent, restart and resume, with no transcript size cap. Transcript
  hydration stays the fallback for chats from before.
- Items: nesting to any depth (parent), notes, an optional owner (subagent
  id), status blocked, up to 1000 items. One in_progress item per owner:
  lanes owned by different subagents may run together.
- Subagents: a narrowed child keeps the todo toolset. list='parent' reads the
  parent's list and updates status and notes of the items assigned to the
  child (or adds subtasks under them). subagent_id reads a child's list,
  running or finished. delegate_task action='list' shows each child's current
  item and counts.
- Compaction: the stored list is loaded before the snapshot is folded in; the
  snapshot shows open items with notes and owners and counts the done ones.
- Gateway: session.todos reads the stored list (or a child's with
  subagent_id); subagent.list rows carry the child's todo brief; a child's
  update of its parent's items, and a messaging route's write, publish
  todo.updated; resumes prefer the stored list.
